        "issues": [
          "**Authorization design.** What information must be shown before a customer authorizes API access, and when must that permission be renewed?",
          "**Migration.** Can existing connections continue until technical reauthentication, or must customers make a new affirmative choice before data continues to flow?",
          "**Purpose limits.** Which uses are necessary for the customer-selected product, and which uses require a separate optional choice?",
          "**Marketing and underwriting.** Should historical transaction data be used to build cross-product offer segments or lending inputs?",
          "**Revocation and deletion.** What must stop when a customer disconnects, and what information may be retained for disputes, fraud, legal duties, or model evidence?",
          "**Regulatory change.** Which design choices remain useful even while the federal section 1033 rule and compliance dates may change?",
          "**Aggregator contract.** Are security, incident notice, subcontractor, purpose, deletion, audit, and transition-assistance terms sufficient?",
          "**Customer support.** Can the company explain connection status, permission, refresh failure, and deletion without sending the customer to the aggregator?"
